the-firm-as-one-program-lines-11 = cons "- **PE** The value is information: everything known before a packet arrives becomes instructions that never run." (cons "  A protocol is defined once, as data. The parser, builder and validator are not written: each is the residual of one generic interpreter specialized on that definition plus everything else that is static. Only operations on the packet bytes remain, and the proofs carried with the specialization hand the C++ optimizer facts it could never infer." nil)
